    "egg": {
      "word": "EGG",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "(Popularly)",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "The oval or roundish body laid by domestic poultry and other birds, tortoises, etc. It consists of a yolk, usually surrounded by the \"white\" or albumen, and inclosed in a shell or strong membrane.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "(Biol.)",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A simple cell, from the development of which the young of animals are formed; ovum; germ cell.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "Anything resembling an egg in form. explaining compounds; as, egg beater or egg-beater, egg case, egg ladle, egg-shaped, etc. Egg and anchor (Arch.), an egg-shaped ornament, alternating with another in the form of a dart, used to",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "To urge on; to instigate; to incite Adam and Eve he egged to ill. Piers Plowman. [She] did egg him on to tell How fair she was. Warner.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        }
      ],
